  "name": "qwen3-8b",
  "description": "The reproduction on Qwen3-8B with the user's own prompts (configs/prompts/my_prompts.txt): every prompt is sent 200 times at temperature 0 to a default vLLM server first, then to a batch-invariant one (VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1), and the completions are compared by token ids and bitwise logprobs. Around that: floating-point demos, op-level run-to-run vs batch invariance in all six kernel modes, model-level invariance with HF transformers, an engine-level needle sweep, prefix caching, and throughput (alone at the end). All prompts come from my_prompts.txt. Roughly 2 h on a GB10.",
